        // and call it "animated thrusters" — but those are two DIFFERENT poses at different
        // dimensions, so the whole ship visibly jerked twice a second while flying straight.
        // The body now holds ONE frame. The thruster animation is the ntr_ trail drawn above,
        // which already cycles 8 authored frames and reacts to throttle. Animate the flame,
        // never the airframe.
        /* THE PLAIN SPRITE IS THE FLAMELESS ONE (drop 0724cj).
           I got this backwards twice. First I counted OPAQUE pixels, which cannot tell a flame
           from a tailfin. Then I counted hot colour and it inverted — ship_<pilot>_t carries the
           MOST flame (lizzie 1218 px, decker 470, yuri 383): _t is the THRUST frame. I was drawing
           the most-lit airframe in the set and overlaying a second thruster on it, which is the
           doubled-up look Mike photographed.
           Confirmed by Mike against a contact sheet of all five variants: ship_<pilot> — the plain
           frame — is the idle airframe with no engine, for every pilot. */
        key = XART.rdy('ship_'+pk) ? ('ship_'+pk) : (XART.rdy('ship_'+pk+'_pv2') ? ('ship_'+pk+'_pv2') : ('ship_'+pk+'_t'));
